            "result_text": "I'll help you set up a git server with automatic deployment to a web server. Here's a complete configuration:\n\n## Server-side setup (run on `server`):\n\n**1. Create a bare git repository:**\n```bash\nmkdir -p /git/server\ngit init --bare /git/server\n```\n\n**2. Create the web directory and post-receive hook:**\n```bash\n# Create web root\nmkdir -p /var/www/html\n\n# Create the post-receive hook\ncat > /git/server/hooks/post-receive << 'EOF'\n#!/bin/bash\nGIT_WORK_TREE=/var/www/html git checkout -f\nEOF\n\n# Make it executable\nchmod +x /git/server/hooks/post-receive\n```\n\n**3. Set up a web server on port 8080:**\n\nUsing Python 3 (simplest):\n```bash\ncd /var/www/html\npython3 -m http.server 8080 &\n```\n\nOr using Node.js with `http-server`:\n```bash\nnpm install -g http-server\ncd /var/www/html\nhttp-server -p 8080\n```\n\nOr using a persistent systemd service with Python. Create `/etc/systemd/system/webserver.service`:\n```ini\n[Unit]\nDescription=Simple HTTP Server on port 8080\nAfter=network.target\n\n[Service]\nType=simple\nWorkingDirectory=/var/www/html\nExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 -m http.server 8080\nRestart=on-failure\n\n[Install]\nWantedBy=multi-user.target\n```\n\nThen enable it:\n```bash\nsudo systemctl daemon-reload\nsudo systemctl enable webserver.service\nsudo systemctl start webserver.service\n```\n\n## Client-side usage (on your computer):\n\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server my-project\ncd my-project\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\n```\n\nThen verify:\n```bash\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html\n# Output: hello world\n```\n\n**How it works:** When you push, the post-receive hook automatically checks out the latest files from the git repo into `/var/www/html`, making them immediately available via the web server."
